WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.340
- So I have to ask, what was
the last day on set like?

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.560
Cause it, that's a big deal.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.179
- Yeah, it was awful, it was awful.

00:00:06.179 --> 00:00:07.012
- [Rachel] It was terrible.

00:00:07.012 --> 00:00:08.160
- A lot of tears.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:08.993
- It was painful.

00:00:08.993 --> 00:00:12.510
I mean, we just all, we
love the show so much.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.470
We love the work.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.040
And we just couldn't quite
wrap our brains around the fact

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.260
that it was coming to a close.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.130
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Rachel] Alex and I.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.200
- I feel like sometimes it
doesn't hit you til afterward.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.550
- Yeah, we had been.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.613
I mean, Alex is a picture of
stoicism most days on set.

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:28.446
(chuckling)

00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:31.292
- Yeah, I'm usually very
cold, and well, kinda mean.

00:00:31.292 --> 00:00:32.160
(laughing)

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.340
- I saw the other word
flash through your eyes.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.173
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:37.290
- You said mean for Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.123
- She kept it daytime.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:38.956
- Yeah, daytime, it's day time.

00:00:38.956 --> 00:00:40.710
- Don't worry, they have
to bleep me all the time.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.543
You're fine.

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:43.890
- But we, we had to
rehearse one of our scenes

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.930
early that morning on the last day.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.880
And we came in and just sort
of stood across from each other

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.870
and we were starting to rehearse.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.570
And Alex was getting teary at
like 8 o'clock in the morning.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.403
- I couldn't look at her.

00:00:52.403 --> 00:00:53.236
I just went like.
- Could not look me

00:00:53.236 --> 00:00:54.180
in the eyes.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.650
And then I couldn't look her in the eyes.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.330
And so we spent all of
our rehearsals, kind of,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.100
I think I was looking at
the center of your forehead

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.150
and you were looking at my--

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.160
- But, to be fair, isn't that usually

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.210
where you have to look at me?

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.333
- You're right, yep. (laughing)

